WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:06.730
HBO is making a Game of Thrones prequel TV
show called House of the Dragon, based on

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:09.290
the Targaryen history book Fire &amp; Blood.

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:14.860
But they’re also developing another prequel
show based on the Tales of Dunk and Egg, a

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:19.590
series of novellas set ninety years before
A Game of Thrones.

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:21.320
Dunk is a young hedge knight.

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:27.339
He’s not particularly smart or skilled but
he’s tall and strong, and he’s determined

00:00:27.339 --> 00:00:28.869
to be an honourable knight.

00:00:28.869 --> 00:00:31.579
Egg is his loyal squire.

00:00:31.579 --> 00:00:37.470
He has a bald head and a big mouth, and he’s
secretly a Targaryen prince, and future king

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:38.710
of Westeros.

00:00:38.710 --> 00:00:43.620
We’ve already made videos about their first
two stories, where Dunk fights in a trial

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:47.460
at a tournament, then in a conflict between
minor lords.

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:53.160
But the third story is called The Mystery
Knight, and it’s a tale of conspiracy, sorcery,

00:00:53.160 --> 00:01:00.460
prophecy, a dragon egg, painted dwarfs, homoerotic
‘jousting’ jokes and a lil baby Walder

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:01.670
Frey.

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:06.190
The Mystery Knight was adapted to a graphic
novel, with art by Mike S Miller.

00:01:06.190 --> 00:01:11.170
At the start of the story, Dunk and Egg are
travelling north towards Winterfell, planning

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:14.540
to help the Starks fight against the ironborn.

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:17.860
This is a time of political tension in Westeros.

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:23.780
Cause the King, Aerys Targaryen, is seen as
“weak”, and he lets his uncle Bloodraven

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:25.910
rule the kingdom for him.

00:01:25.910 --> 00:01:31.979
Many people hate Bloodraven – they call
him a sorcerer, a bastard.. and a kinslayer.

00:01:31.979 --> 00:01:38.060
Cause sixteen years ago, Bloodraven’s half-brother
Daemon Blackfyre, started a rebellion to take

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:39.060
the Throne.

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:45.120
But at the Battle of the Redgrass Field, Bloodraven
killed his half-brother in a hail of arrows,

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:48.950
and Daemon’s surviving sons fled east across
the sea.

00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:54.010
Now, sixteen years later, some people want
the Blackfyres to return.

00:01:54.010 --> 00:02:00.980
Dunk and Egg see a preacher who says Bloodraven
is evil and the Blackfyres should rule Westeros.

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:05.950
Bloodraven doesn’t tolerate treason – so
he has the preacher killed.

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:12.019
Bloodraven has spies all over Westeros, it’s
said he has “A thousand eyes, and one”

00:02:12.019 --> 00:02:17.799
–one eye on his face, cause he lost an eye
in the Blackfyre Rebellion, and the thousand

00:02:17.799 --> 00:02:20.440
eyes of his spies.

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:26.819
Dunk and Egg take care while travelling, cause
there are “perilous times”.

00:02:26.819 --> 00:02:32.650
Also, Egg gets a new hat, and he gives his
old hat to their mule, and even cuts out little

00:02:32.650 --> 00:02:35.079
holes cut out for his ears, which is adorable.

00:02:35.079 --> 00:02:41.109
The mule is named Maester, because it was
given to them by Egg’s brother, a young

00:02:41.109 --> 00:02:43.189
Maester Aemon.

00:02:43.189 --> 00:02:48.749
On the road, Dunk and Egg meet a group of
lords – there’s Gormon Peake, Alyn Cockshaw,

00:02:48.749 --> 00:02:52.379
and this guy who calls himself “John the
Fiddler”.

00:02:52.379 --> 00:02:57.239
Peake and Cockshaw are both rude to Dunk,
but the Fiddler is friendly.

00:02:57.239 --> 00:03:02.860
He says he’s a humble travelling hedge knight,
like Dunk, all like ‘how do you do, “fellow

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:03.860
hedge knights”’.

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:08.909
But he wears rich clothes, and talks like
a lord, so he’s obviously not who he says

00:03:08.909 --> 00:03:13.219
he is – the Fiddler and his friends are
up to something.

00:03:13.219 --> 00:03:17.859
The Fiddler hits on Dunk – admiring how
“large” Dunk is, saying he would love

00:03:17.859 --> 00:03:24.019
to “cross swords” with Dunk, and wants
to try his lance on him, but Dunk is oblivious

00:03:24.019 --> 00:03:25.569
to the flirting.

00:03:25.569 --> 00:03:30.709
The Fiddler is going to a castle called Whitewalls,
for a wedding and a tournament held by Lord

00:03:30.709 --> 00:03:31.829
Butterwell.

00:03:31.829 --> 00:03:36.650
So Dunk and Egg head there too – they hope
to win some money at the jousting, and eat

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:39.069
some good food at the feast.

00:03:39.069 --> 00:03:41.370
Along the way, they meet some knights.

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:47.909
There’s Kyle the Cat who has “ginger whiskers”,
like a cat, a mysterious man called Maynard

00:03:47.909 --> 00:03:52.690
Plumm, and a proud young knight called Glendon
Ball.

00:03:52.690 --> 00:03:59.230
Glendon says he’s the son of Quentyn Ball,
a famous knight nicknamed “Fireball”.

00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:03.799
Fireball was the master-at-arms who taught
young Targaryens how to fight – he trained

00:04:03.799 --> 00:04:10.459
King Aerys, and Egg’s father Maekar, and
taught Bloodraven and Daemon Blackfyre.

00:04:10.459 --> 00:04:16.400
When Daemon started his rebellion, Fireball
joined the Blackfyres, but died before the

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:17.979
Redgrass Field.

00:04:17.979 --> 00:04:23.120
Glendon hopes to prove himself as a great
knight like Fireball by winning the tournament

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:28.419
at Whitewalls, and getting the grand prize
– a dragon egg.

00:04:28.419 --> 00:04:33.979
The last dragon died sixty years ago, and
the remaining dragon eggs haven’t hatched

00:04:33.979 --> 00:04:34.979
since.

00:04:34.979 --> 00:04:40.640
So a famously unworthy king called Aegon the
Unworthy once gave a dragon egg to a Lord

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:44.250
Butterwell in return for his daughters.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:49.389
Now, Lord Butterwell is offering this egg
as a tournament prize, and Dunk wonders why

00:04:49.389 --> 00:04:52.919
he’d give away something so valuable.

00:04:52.919 --> 00:04:57.270
At Whitewalls, Lord Butterwell marries a daughter
of Lord Frey.

00:04:57.270 --> 00:05:02.979
We also see Lord Frey’s four-year-old son,
who ninety years later, grows up to be Lord

00:05:02.979 --> 00:05:05.639
Walder Frey in the main series.

00:05:05.639 --> 00:05:10.800
Dunk says this kid is “snot-nosed” and
“hideous”, and has such an “irritating

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:14.300
laugh” that he wants to throw the boy down
a well.

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:19.060
If he did, then maybe the Red Wedding wouldn’t
have happened, ninety years later.

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:24.150
The lords propose toasts to the bride and
groom, to the king, and to the king’s Hand,

00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:25.150
Bloodraven.

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:29.629
But many at the feast hate Bloodraven and
refuse to toast him.

00:05:29.629 --> 00:05:35.419
And when they toast to the king, Glendon holds
his wine cup over a basin of water.

00:05:35.419 --> 00:05:38.759
This is a reference to a real historical practice.

00:05:38.759 --> 00:05:44.280
In the 1700s, Britain was ruled by House Hanover,
but a group called the Jacobites wanted the

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:46.280
Stuarts to be king.

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:49.879
Charles Stuart lived in exile overseas in
France [and elsewhere in continental Europe].

00:05:49.879 --> 00:05:54.730
So when the Jacobites toasted to the king,
they held their cups over water to show that

00:05:54.730 --> 00:05:59.290
their king is Charles Stuart, the king ‘over
the water'.

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:04.189
In The Mystery Knight, Glendon does the same
thing, showing that he supports the Blackfyres

00:06:04.189 --> 00:06:06.939
‘over the water’ in Essos.

00:06:06.939 --> 00:06:11.740
Real history inspired a lot of this series.

00:06:11.740 --> 00:06:17.169
So Dunk and Egg start to realise that many
people at this tournament support the Blackfyres,

00:06:17.169 --> 00:06:22.690
not the Targaryens – Egg says “This is
a traitors’ tourney”.

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:28.050
Still, Dunk enjoys the feast, and drinks a
lot, and when he goes out for a piss, he overhears

00:06:28.050 --> 00:06:33.889
a conversation between Gormon Peake, and Butterwell’s
son-in-law, “Black” Tom Heddle.

00:06:33.889 --> 00:06:38.500
Tom complains that they don’t have Bittersteel’s
support.

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:43.009
Bittersteel is the half-brother of Daemon
Blackfyre, and was one of his main supporters

00:06:43.009 --> 00:06:45.009
in the Blackfyre Rebellion.

00:06:45.009 --> 00:06:50.129
When Daemon was killed, Bittersteel went east
with Daemon’s sons, and has plotted invasion

00:06:50.129 --> 00:06:52.699
of Westeros ever since.

00:06:52.699 --> 00:06:57.879
Peake says they don’t need Bittersteel’s
help, because their prince had a dream that

00:06:57.879 --> 00:07:00.690
the dragon egg will hatch.

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:08.750
So Peake and Black Tom and Lord Butterwell
and Frey are plotting a second Blackfyre rebellion.

00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:13.590
This whole tournament and wedding is an excuse
to bring together Blackfyre supporters, to

00:07:13.590 --> 00:07:15.729
kick off a war for the throne.

00:07:15.729 --> 00:07:20.030
But who is their prince with these dreams?

00:07:20.030 --> 00:07:25.050
At the feast, some dwarfs perform, and Dunk
carries the bride to her bedding.

00:07:25.050 --> 00:07:30.849
Dunk is really drunk by then, so he goes for
some air, and finds John the Fiddler.

00:07:30.849 --> 00:07:37.349
The Fiddler is also pretty wasted, and he
says that his dreams come true – like, he

00:07:37.349 --> 00:07:41.550
once dreamed that his brothers would die and
then they died.

00:07:41.550 --> 00:07:47.440
He also had a dream that Dunk will join the
Kingsguard, the greatest knights in the realm.

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:51.689
And he dreamed that a dragon egg will hatch
at Whitewalls.

00:07:51.689 --> 00:07:56.960
The Fiddler believes he will win the dragon
egg at this tournament, hatch a dragon, and

00:07:56.960 --> 00:08:01.500
become the king of Westeros, with Dunk in
his Kingsguard.

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:05.569
So the Fiddler is the prince in Peake’s
conspiracy.

00:08:05.569 --> 00:08:12.029
Cause his real name is Daemon Blackfyre the
Second, son of Daemon the First – he came

00:08:12.029 --> 00:08:16.469
across the sea to start a new war for the
throne.

00:08:16.469 --> 00:08:21.410
And there were hints of this earlier – the
Fiddler gives a toast to his “brave brothers”,

00:08:21.410 --> 00:08:24.389
which refers to his dead Blackfyre brothers.

00:08:24.389 --> 00:08:29.650
The Fiddler smells of “eastern spice”
– because he just came across from Essos

00:08:29.650 --> 00:08:30.830
in the east.

00:08:30.830 --> 00:08:37.520
The Fiddler dyes his hair black to hide the
blonde, but his eyes are the purple of Targaryens

00:08:37.520 --> 00:08:39.130
and Blackfyres.

00:08:39.130 --> 00:08:44.550
Peake shuts up the Fiddler before he gives
away their whole conspiracy, and Dunk falls

00:08:44.550 --> 00:08:46.440
into bed.

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:51.680
In the morning, it’s hot, Dunk is super
hung over, he barely remembers that Blackfyre

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:56.600
stuff, and he just wants to get through the
jousting tournament without throwing up.

00:08:56.600 --> 00:09:01.580
Dunk isn’t actually very good at jousting
with a lance – he’s better with a sword

00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:02.580
in a fight.

00:09:02.580 --> 00:09:06.480
But he just needs to win two jousts to make
some money.

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:12.870
His first opponent is some guy called Uthor
the Snail, so like how tough can he be, right?

00:09:12.870 --> 00:09:19.520
Dunk and the Snail charge at each other, and
Dunk.. gets smashed in the head really hard,

00:09:19.520 --> 00:09:21.140
and falls down.

00:09:21.140 --> 00:09:26.130
Dunk wakes up hours later with the mother
of all headaches, but alive.

00:09:26.130 --> 00:09:30.880
He says hi to the dwarfs from the feast last
night, and one of them smells like a toilet

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:34.660
which is weird…? but Dunk has bigger problems.

00:09:34.660 --> 00:09:39.640
Cause at this tournament, when you’re defeated
in a joust, the knight who beat you gets your

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:44.930
horse and sword and armour, and you’ve got
to pay a ransom to get your stuff back.

00:09:44.930 --> 00:09:51.040
But Dunk lost his first joust, and he doesn’t
have the money for a ransom, so.. it looks

00:09:51.040 --> 00:09:54.430
like his life as a knight is over.

00:09:54.430 --> 00:09:58.640
Maynard Plumm says Dunk should just keep his
stuff and run.

00:09:58.640 --> 00:10:00.480
But Dunk refuses to cheat.

00:10:00.480 --> 00:10:04.340
So he gives his stuff to Uthor the Snail.

00:10:04.340 --> 00:10:10.100
Uthor’s tent looks plain from the outside,
but inside, it’s luxurious and comfortable

00:10:10.100 --> 00:10:15.040
– Uthor lurks inside here like a snail in
his shell.

00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:19.540
It turns out that Uthor is like a professional
jousting grifter.

00:10:19.540 --> 00:10:24.270
Cause he’s really good at jousting, but
he hides his skill.

00:10:24.270 --> 00:10:29.500
He deliberately never wins tournaments, only
getting second or third prize, so that people

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:31.600
always underestimate him.

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:36.820
And he bribes the people running this tournament
so he goes up against knights who look tough

00:10:36.820 --> 00:10:44.570
but actually suck, so the Snail and his squire
can make money by taking bets against himself.

00:10:44.570 --> 00:10:49.200
Uthor offers to give Dunk his arms back if
he joins in on Uthor’s con.

00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:55.990
But Dunk refuses this dishonesty and corruption
– he’d rather give up his knighthood than

00:10:55.990 --> 00:10:57.270
his honour.

00:10:57.270 --> 00:11:03.930
Uthor tells Dunk the story of Glendon Ball,
the kid who says he’s the son of Fireball.

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:09.170
Apparently, Glendon’s mother was a camp
follower called Penny Jenny who was with so

00:11:09.170 --> 00:11:14.970
many soldiers that there’s no way of knowing
if Fireball really is Glendon’s father.

00:11:14.970 --> 00:11:20.930
Glendon was raised in a brothel, and he was
only knighted.. in return for a knight having

00:11:20.930 --> 00:11:22.580
his sister.

00:11:22.580 --> 00:11:29.480
So all the lords at this tournament look down
on Glendon as the baseborn son of a whore,

00:11:29.480 --> 00:11:30.950
knighted dishonourably.

00:11:30.950 --> 00:11:37.210
Glendon hoped to win some respect in the jousting
– cause Glendon is really talented knight.

00:11:37.210 --> 00:11:44.620
But no matter how many times he proves his
skill, the lords still treat him like trash.

00:11:44.620 --> 00:11:50.270
Dunk sympathises – he’s often been treated
the same way, as a bastard orphan from Flea

00:11:50.270 --> 00:11:51.270
Bottom.

00:11:51.270 --> 00:11:56.820
It’s so unfair that in this class system,
people are judged by who their parents were

00:11:56.820 --> 00:11:59.950
instead of by their actions and their talent.

00:11:59.950 --> 00:12:05.290
As a Japanese philosopher once said, “the
circumstances of one's birth are irrelevant;

00:12:05.290 --> 00:12:10.070
it is what you do with the gift of life that
determines who you are”.

00:12:10.070 --> 00:12:14.570
It's ironic that Glendon and Dunk treated
like they’re not real knights, when these

00:12:14.570 --> 00:12:18.370
guys are practically the only honest honourable
knights here.

00:12:18.370 --> 00:12:23.980
Uthor has his jousting grift, Maynard says
to break the rules, Kyle the Cat deliberately

00:12:23.980 --> 00:12:26.560
loses his joust to suck up to a lord.

00:12:26.560 --> 00:12:32.420
And it turns out that Peake is bribing people
to make sure Daemon wins the tournament.

00:12:32.420 --> 00:12:37.740
But when he tries to bribe Glendon to lose
to Daemon, Glendon refuses.

00:12:37.740 --> 00:12:44.360
So Glendon might not really be Quentyn Ball’s
son, and Dunk might not really have been knighted

00:12:44.360 --> 00:12:46.150
in his first story.

00:12:46.150 --> 00:12:51.990
But these guys are the truest knights here,
and they become friends.

00:12:51.990 --> 00:12:57.460
As the jousting continues, rain falls down
from dark ominous clouds.

00:12:57.460 --> 00:13:03.180
Butterwell’s dragon egg mysteriously goes
missing, so Peake falsely accuses Glendon

00:13:03.180 --> 00:13:04.830
of stealing it.

00:13:04.830 --> 00:13:10.320
And then a different egg goes missing – Dunk’s
squire Egg.. disappears.

00:13:10.320 --> 00:13:16.420
Alyn Cockshaw says he knows where to find
Egg, so Dunk follows him into a trap.

00:13:16.420 --> 00:13:22.680
It turns out, Alyn is in love with Daemon,
they’d had a relationship for years – and

00:13:22.680 --> 00:13:28.940
it’s hinted that Daemon being gay was why
Bittersteel didn’t support his rebellion.

00:13:28.940 --> 00:13:34.020
But Alyn is jealous that Daemon now wants
Dunk instead of him.

00:13:34.020 --> 00:13:39.790
So Alyn actually paid Uthor to kill Dunk in
the joust, and that’s why he hit Dunk in

00:13:39.790 --> 00:13:41.050
the head.

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:44.170
Since that didn’t work, Alyn tries to kill
Dunk himself.

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:50.260
He attacks Dunk with a dagger, so Dunk beats
him with a rock, and throws him down a well.

00:13:50.260 --> 00:13:56.240
The excellent Radio Westeros podcast points
out that this fight between Dunk and Alyn

00:13:56.240 --> 00:14:01.600
is similar to a fight in the main books between
Brienne and a guy called Shagwell, which also

00:14:01.600 --> 00:14:05.400
involves a dagger and a rock and a well.

00:14:05.400 --> 00:14:10.760
In Dunk’s fight, rock beats dagger, but
in Brienne’s fight dagger beats rock – it’s

00:14:10.760 --> 00:14:12.910
like rock paper scissors.

00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:18.380
And in the previous Dunk and Egg story, Dunk
fought a man in a stream – which is similar

00:14:18.380 --> 00:14:23.860
to Brienne’s fight with Jaime, which, in
the books, happens in a stream.

00:14:23.860 --> 00:14:29.040
And in the first Dunk and Egg story, Dunk
defeats Aerion in a similar way to how Brienne

00:14:29.040 --> 00:14:35.520
defeats Loras Tyrell – by knocking him down,
raising his visor, and making him yield.

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:41.160
So in each of these three fights, Brienne’s
story echoes Dunk’s story.

00:14:41.160 --> 00:14:45.870
Which makes sense, because author George Martin
has said that Dunk and Brienne are related

00:14:45.870 --> 00:14:46.870
– he might be her great-grandfather.

00:14:46.870 --> 00:14:52.330
Dunk and Brienne are both tall powerful warriors
who travel Westeros with their loyal squires

00:14:52.330 --> 00:14:58.870
by their sides, struggling to be true knights
in a society that looks down on them.

00:14:58.870 --> 00:15:05.420
So Dunk kills Alyn, then suddenly Maynard
Plumm appears, and helps Dunk with his wound.

00:15:05.420 --> 00:15:11.780
Maynard seems to know all about Daemon and
Peake’s conspiracy, but only gives hints

00:15:11.780 --> 00:15:14.780
at his own motives and identity.

00:15:14.780 --> 00:15:18.290
He tells Dunk to find Egg in the sept.

00:15:18.290 --> 00:15:23.860
Egg had wanted to help Dunk, and to prevent
this Blackfyre rebellion against his family

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:30.020
the Targaryens, so Egg went to Butterwell,
and revealed his true identity as Prince Aegon

00:15:30.020 --> 00:15:36.440
Targaryen, and threatened him with attack
and execution – Egg acts with the confidence

00:15:36.440 --> 00:15:38.950
and courage of a prince.

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:44.410
Black Tom Heddle tries to take Egg hostage,
so he and Dunk have a big fight, and Dunk

00:15:44.410 --> 00:15:49.290
proves that he really is better with a sword
than with a lance.

00:15:49.290 --> 00:15:53.820
It's hitting the fan, so Dunk tells Egg to
ride for safety.

00:15:53.820 --> 00:16:00.030
But Dunk walks right up to Daemon, in front
of everyone, reveals his conspiracy, and demands

00:16:00.030 --> 00:16:02.910
“Justice” “for Glendon Ball”.

00:16:02.910 --> 00:16:07.710
Dunk knows it’s super dangerous for him
to publicly oppose Lord Peake.

00:16:07.710 --> 00:16:13.550
He’s standing alone against a deadly political
conspiracy, to protect this bloke Glendon

00:16:13.550 --> 00:16:15.050
who he barely knows.

00:16:15.050 --> 00:16:19.660
Uthor asks if Dunk is gallant or just stupid.

00:16:19.660 --> 00:16:25.080
But to Dunk, foolishness and heroism are sometimes
the same thing.

00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:31.220
In his first story, Tanselle said “All men
are fools, and all men are knights”.

00:16:31.220 --> 00:16:38.360
Fighting against impossible odds to help others
is foolish, but it’s also true heroism.

00:16:38.360 --> 00:16:44.810
Luckily, Daemon wants the truth – he didn’t
know that Peake was rigging the tournament

00:16:44.810 --> 00:16:45.810
for him.

00:16:45.810 --> 00:16:51.390
So Daemon challenges Glendon to a trial by
combat to decide his innocence.

00:16:51.390 --> 00:16:55.050
Glendon was “savagely” tortured in the
dungeon.

00:16:55.050 --> 00:17:01.350
He’s burned and beaten, missing teeth and
fingernails, and now, to win his life, he’s

00:17:01.350 --> 00:17:03.990
got to defeat Daemon Blackfyre.

00:17:03.990 --> 00:17:09.860
Glendon laughs at the irony, cause Glendon
wanted to fight for the Blackfyres, just as

00:17:09.860 --> 00:17:11.870
his father Fireball had.

00:17:11.870 --> 00:17:14.640
Glendon would have joined Daemon if he’d
asked.

00:17:14.640 --> 00:17:20.420
But since Glendon had refused to cheat and
lose for this conspiracy, now he’s gotta

00:17:20.420 --> 00:17:22.630
fight against Daemon.

00:17:22.630 --> 00:17:28.400
Daemon washes out his hair dye, and reveals
his Blackfyre colours, looking just like his

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:30.520
father Daemon the First.

00:17:30.520 --> 00:17:36.440
Glendon has a fireball on his shield, just
like his supposed father, Quentyn.

00:17:36.440 --> 00:17:40.450
The story asks “is the boy his father’s
son?”

00:17:40.450 --> 00:17:43.320
Is Glendon a great knight like Fireball?

00:17:43.320 --> 00:17:48.400
Is Daemon a true warrior and leader like his
father, Daemon the First?

00:17:48.400 --> 00:17:53.560
The two knights crash together, and Daemon
Blackfyre splats into the mud.

00:17:53.560 --> 00:17:57.900
The crowd laughs, and calls him “The Brown
Dragon”.

00:17:57.900 --> 00:18:04.040
So Daemon the Second is not a warrior and
leader like his father Daemon the First.

00:18:04.040 --> 00:18:10.810
But Glendon is a great knight like Fireball,
even though Fireball probably isn’t Glendon’s

00:18:10.810 --> 00:18:11.810
father.

00:18:11.810 --> 00:18:17.540
It’s like how Jon Snow isn’t Ned Stark’s
son, but he does embody Ned’s values and

00:18:17.540 --> 00:18:18.720
legacy.

00:18:18.720 --> 00:18:23.340
So maybe greatness and family isn’t in your
blood.

00:18:23.340 --> 00:18:25.960
Maybe it’s something you can choose.

00:18:25.960 --> 00:18:33.040
Suddenly, a Targaryen army arrives to crush
this rebellion, led by the Hand of the King,

00:18:33.040 --> 00:18:34.070
Bloodraven himself.

00:18:34.070 --> 00:18:40.600
Daemon tries to rally the castle to fight
Bloodraven, to rise up in a second Blackfyre

00:18:40.600 --> 00:18:41.600
rebellion.

00:18:41.600 --> 00:18:45.950
But Daemon’s cause seems hopeless and false.

00:18:45.950 --> 00:18:51.600
He didn’t win his tournament, it was rigged,
and got beat into the mud by a bastard boy

00:18:51.600 --> 00:18:52.600
anyway.

00:18:52.600 --> 00:18:57.440
He doesn’t have a dragon egg, or the dragon
he said would hatch.

00:18:57.440 --> 00:18:59.690
He doesn’t have Bittersteel, or an army.

00:18:59.690 --> 00:19:04.950
And he doesn’t have the legendary sword
Blackfyre, the sword that gave Daemon the

00:19:04.950 --> 00:19:07.060
First his name.

00:19:07.060 --> 00:19:14.220
Politics in Westeros is about symbols of power
and legitimacy, and Daemon has nothing.

00:19:14.220 --> 00:19:18.780
So in the end, Daemon rides out alone against
Bloodraven.

00:19:18.780 --> 00:19:22.640
Bloodraven arrests Daemon, and burns his Blackfyre
flag.

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:28.790
“The First Blackfyre Rebellion had perished
on the Redgrass Field in blood and glory.

00:19:28.790 --> 00:19:33.400
The Second Blackfyre Rebellion ended with
a whimper”.

00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:38.580
Bloodraven arrests everyone, and decides who
to pardon and who to kill.

00:19:38.580 --> 00:19:43.130
He spares Butterwell, but takes his money,
and destroys his castle.

00:19:43.130 --> 00:19:45.020
And he kills Lord Peake.

00:19:45.020 --> 00:19:50.290
Daemon he keeps as a prisoner, cause so long
as he’s alive, his younger brothers in Essos

00:19:50.290 --> 00:19:53.340
can’t claim to be the new Blackfyre king.

00:19:53.340 --> 00:19:58.880
Lord Frey, who married his daughter to Lord
Butterwell, and seemed involved in the conspiracy,

00:19:58.880 --> 00:20:04.160
doesn’t get punished, and seems friendly
with Bloodraven – it looks like he might

00:20:04.160 --> 00:20:08.450
have switched sides to inform on the conspiracy
to Bloodraven.

00:20:08.450 --> 00:20:13.260
So even ninety years ago, you can’t trust
a bloody Frey.

00:20:13.260 --> 00:20:17.370
Then Dunk faces Bloodraven’s judgement.

00:20:17.370 --> 00:20:21.370
Bloodraven got his name from the raven-shaped
birthmark on his face.

00:20:21.370 --> 00:20:28.110
He’s an albino, with red eyes, and his skin
and hair are white as bone.

00:20:28.110 --> 00:20:33.940
Bloodraven looks similar to Elric of Melniboné,
a fantasy character by Michael Moorcock who

00:20:33.940 --> 00:20:45.240
is also a warrior and sorcerer, with red eyes,
and skin and hair that’s bone white.

00:20:45.240 --> 00:20:49.760
Bloodraven asks what the hell Dunk and Prince
Egg were doing here in the middle of this

00:20:49.760 --> 00:20:51.050
rebellion.

00:20:51.050 --> 00:20:56.600
Dunk says they just sorta accidentally wandered
into it, but Egg says they had it all under

00:20:56.600 --> 00:20:57.600
control.

00:20:57.600 --> 00:21:02.820
Egg demands gold so Dunk can buy back his
arms and armour, and demands that Glendon

00:21:02.820 --> 00:21:05.340
should be released, and rewarded.

00:21:05.340 --> 00:21:12.050
Egg finds new confidence in this story – confronting
Butterwell, revealing his identity, acting

00:21:12.050 --> 00:21:13.610
like a prince.

00:21:13.610 --> 00:21:19.400
And Bloodraven says that this fulfils Daemon’s
dream about a dragon hatching – it wasn’t

00:21:19.400 --> 00:21:23.100
a literal dragon hatching from a literal egg.

00:21:23.100 --> 00:21:31.040
The egg was Egg, and the dragon is his new
confidence as Prince Aegon Targaryen.

00:21:31.040 --> 00:21:33.960
But what happened to the actual dragon egg?

00:21:33.960 --> 00:21:35.490
Who stole it?

00:21:35.490 --> 00:21:40.860
Bloodraven reveals that those dwarfs who performed
at the feast worked for him, and one of them

00:21:40.860 --> 00:21:45.350
climbed up through a toilet, to steal the
dragon egg for Bloodraven.

00:21:45.350 --> 00:21:49.420
That foul-smelling dwarf who Dunk saw was
the thief.

00:21:49.420 --> 00:21:55.559
So Dunk and Egg ride off into the sunset,
but there’s another mystery the story doesn’t

00:21:55.559 --> 00:21:56.559
answer.

00:21:56.559 --> 00:21:59.000
- the mysterious Maynard Plumm.

00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:00.080
What was he up to?

00:22:00.080 --> 00:22:06.770
He’s this knowing, watching figure throughout
the story, but at the end, he disappears – right

00:22:06.770 --> 00:22:09.730
before Bloodraven arrives.

00:22:09.730 --> 00:22:14.340
Dunk notices there’s something strange about
Maynard’s face.

00:22:14.340 --> 00:22:20.020
For one moment, he appears as “a hooded
shape” with “a single pale” eye.

00:22:20.020 --> 00:22:26.000
It’s implied that Maynard Plumm is actually
Bloodraven in disguise.

00:22:26.000 --> 00:22:29.290
Cause Bloodraven is said to be a sorcerer.

00:22:29.290 --> 00:22:34.880
That he can “change his face”, and that
crows and wolves spy for him.

00:22:34.880 --> 00:22:41.140
Which is probably true, cause ninety years
later, Bloodraven becomes the three-eyed crow,

00:22:41.140 --> 00:22:46.780
a magical greenseer who trains Bran to control
animals to spy.

00:22:46.780 --> 00:22:52.690
And when Dunk and Egg meet Maynard, he’s
in a grove of weirwood stumps, and weirwoods

00:22:52.690 --> 00:22:55.530
are connected to the magic of the old gods.

00:22:55.530 --> 00:23:01.670
Butterwell’s castle has rafters made of
weirwood, which might also hint that Bloodraven

00:23:01.670 --> 00:23:03.020
is watching.

00:23:03.020 --> 00:23:09.440
But Bloodraven’s disguise as Maynard is
probably a kind of magic called a glamour.

00:23:09.440 --> 00:23:15.300
In the main books, Melisandre magically disguises
Mance Rayder to look like Rattleshirt.

00:23:15.300 --> 00:23:18.800
And this magic is connected to a ruby Mance
wears.

00:23:18.800 --> 00:23:25.510
Similarly, Maynard wears this giant moonstone
brooch, which might be the key to his magical

00:23:25.510 --> 00:23:26.780
disguise.

00:23:26.780 --> 00:23:33.420
So all this time, Bloodraven, the Hand of
the King, was watching the treason and conspiracy

00:23:33.420 --> 00:23:40.010
at Whitewalls, learning who the traitors are,
securing the dragon egg, deciding who to execute

00:23:40.010 --> 00:23:41.010
later.

00:23:41.010 --> 00:23:45.140
But at the same time, he’s having a whole
lotta fun.

00:23:45.140 --> 00:23:48.030
He drinks and gossips and jokes.

00:23:48.030 --> 00:23:53.600
He jokes that maybe he’s the son of Aegon
Targaryen the Fourth, when Bloodraven really

00:23:53.600 --> 00:23:56.830
is a bastard son of Aegon the Fourth.

00:23:56.830 --> 00:24:02.070
He says the north is “too cold” for him,
which is funny cause Bloodraven later goes

00:24:02.070 --> 00:24:04.900
far north beyond the Wall.

00:24:04.900 --> 00:24:12.370
At the feast, Maynard makes crude jokes about
teats, and he calls Lord Butterwell “Lord

00:24:12.370 --> 00:24:13.530
Butterbutt”.

00:24:13.530 --> 00:24:19.400
Bloodraven is a ruthless politician spying
on his enemies, but he’s also a magical

00:24:19.400 --> 00:24:23.280
trickster dressing up and getting on the beers
with the boys.

00:24:23.280 --> 00:24:30.210
It’s a lot like the Norse god Odin, who
also had one eye, and spied with ravens, and

00:24:30.210 --> 00:24:35.260
liked to magically disguise himself as a mortal
and make jokes about titties.

00:24:35.260 --> 00:24:42.160
So you can see inspiration from mythology,
fantasy, and real-life history in this story.

00:24:42.160 --> 00:24:46.890
The story also reveals the dangers of dreams
and prophecies.

00:24:46.890 --> 00:24:53.130
Daemon is convinced that his rebellion will
succeed because of his dragon dreams – and

00:24:53.130 --> 00:24:58.660
his dreams do come true, but not in the way
he expected – cause the hatching dragon

00:24:58.660 --> 00:25:01.920
egg is actually a metaphor for Prince Egg.

00:25:01.920 --> 00:25:08.780
And yeah, Dunk does eventually join the Kingsguard,
but he guards King Egg, not King Daemon.

00:25:08.780 --> 00:25:15.120
Daemon’s dreams don’t lie, he just misinterprets
them, believes what he wants to believe.

00:25:15.120 --> 00:25:18.130
And this happens all throughout the series.

00:25:18.130 --> 00:25:23.620
Melisandre convinces herself that Stannis
is the prophesied hero Azor Ahai.

00:25:23.620 --> 00:25:29.700
And she mistakes a vision of Alys Karstark
for a vision of Arya – the vision was true,

00:25:29.700 --> 00:25:32.010
but her reading was false.

00:25:32.010 --> 00:25:38.210
Cersei thinks the prophecy of Maggy the Frog
means that Margaery and Tyrion will destroy

00:25:38.210 --> 00:25:43.890
her – but it might actually be Daenerys
and Jaime and Cersei’s own self-destructiveness

00:25:43.890 --> 00:25:45.550
that will destroy her.

00:25:45.550 --> 00:25:51.350
And the Targaryens have been tormented by
dreams and prophecies for centuries – King

00:25:51.350 --> 00:25:57.420
Aerys, King Jaehaerys, Maester Aemon, and
Rhaegar, were all obsessed with prophecy,

00:25:57.420 --> 00:26:02.730
hoping to bring back the dragons or the prince
that was promised to save the world.

00:26:02.730 --> 00:26:08.860
But Aemon says that all of his brothers were
killed by their dragon dreams.

00:26:08.860 --> 00:26:14.740
Daeron drank himself to oblivion, Aerion drank
wildfire thinking it’ll transform him into

00:26:14.740 --> 00:26:21.970
a dragon, and Egg had dragon dreams that led
to death at Summerhall – but that’s a

00:26:21.970 --> 00:26:24.070
story for another video.

00:26:24.070 --> 00:26:30.490
And above it all, for a hundred years, Bloodraven
has watched over House Targaryen, ruthlessly

00:26:30.490 --> 00:26:34.300
protecting the royal bloodline from the Blackfyres.

00:26:34.300 --> 00:26:37.530
What dreams and prophecies has he seen?

00:26:37.530 --> 00:26:43.940
And what do they mean for the destiny of Daenerys
and Jon Snow, the last of the Targaryen bloodline,

00:26:43.940 --> 00:26:48.820
who themselves have prophetic dreams of fighting
the dead with fire?

00:26:48.820 --> 00:26:55.879
If Dunk and Egg is anything to go by, their
dreams don’t mean what we think.

00:26:55.879 --> 00:27:00.500
The Mystery Knight is the third and final
of the published Dunk and Egg stories, but

00:27:00.500 --> 00:27:05.640
author George Martin plans to write more,
maybe ten or twelve to tell the whole life

00:27:05.640 --> 00:27:08.000
stories of Dunk and Egg.

00:27:08.000 --> 00:27:13.230
He says possible future titles include “The
She-Wolves of Winterfell” about the Starks

00:27:13.230 --> 00:27:18.770
in the north, which some fans think might
involve a romance between Dunk and a young

00:27:18.770 --> 00:27:19.770
Old Nan.

00:27:19.770 --> 00:27:26.230
“The Village Hero” is set in the Riverlands,
and might involve the infamous Brute of Bracken.

00:27:26.230 --> 00:27:31.820
“The Champion” might be about Dunk’s
fight against the Laughing Storm, Lyonel Baratheon.

00:27:31.820 --> 00:27:36.980
“The Kingsguard” and “The Lord Commander”
might be about Dunk in King Egg’s Kingsguard.

00:27:36.980 --> 00:27:43.310
There are still three more Blackfyre rebellions
to cover, and the story of how Egg became

00:27:43.310 --> 00:27:44.310
king.

00:27:44.310 --> 00:27:50.010
Dunk might reunite with his crush Tanselle,
or with Rohanne, or get revenge on Bennis.

00:27:50.010 --> 00:27:55.250
There’re lots of possibilities for future
Dunk and Egg stories, and maybe their final

00:27:55.250 --> 00:27:58.970
tale will end with Summerhall.

00:27:58.970 --> 00:28:03.360
For now there are three published stories,
and you can get all of them on audiobook for

00:28:03.360 --> 00:28:05.600
free right now at audible.com/asx.

00:28:05.600 --> 00:28:12.640
A Knight of the Seven Kingdoms includes all
three Dunk and Egg stories, read on audiobook

00:28:12.640 --> 00:28:16.690
by Harry Lloyd, the actor who played Viserys
on Game of Thrones.

00:28:16.690 --> 00:28:21.880
Or you could get Dune, or His Dark Materials,
or The Expanse.

00:28:21.880 --> 00:28:27.390
Just sign up for a Premium Plus trial membership,
and you get an audiobook to keep, even if

00:28:27.390 --> 00:28:29.580
you cancel the trial later.

00:28:29.580 --> 00:28:33.990
Membership also includes unlimited access
to thousands of audiobooks and shows in the

00:28:33.990 --> 00:28:35.720
Audible Plus Catalog.

00:28:35.720 --> 00:28:41.970
The trial is free, so it’s a pretty good
deal – sign up at audible.com/asx, or text

00:28:41.970 --> 00:28:45.000
asx to 500-500.

00:28:45.000 --> 00:28:50.160
Thanks for watching, and thanks to the Patrons,
including Matthew Mchale, Monty, Owen Jones,

00:28:50.160 --> 00:28:54.100
Luca Maragò Savorelli, Mike Batko, and Willy
Hardy.

00:28:54.100 --> 00:28:54.679
Cheers.

